[{:adr/id 2790003355, :adr/title "cloud-itonami-isco-3355 — Police Inspectors and Detectives Case-File Documentation and Administrative-Logistics Coordination Coverage", :adr/status :accepted, :adr/date "2026-07-17", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/source-format "edn", :adr/scope [:kotoba-lang/occupation :cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-3355], :adr/references [2607121000 2607152500], :adr/related ["adr-2790003353-cloud-itonami-isco-3353-social-benefits-officials-coverage"], :actor/id :cloud-itonami-isco-3355, :actor/name "Police Case-File Documentation and Administrative-Logistics Coordination Practice", :actor/domain :public-safety/case-file-documentation-and-logistics-coordination, :actor/isco-08 "3355", :actor/wave 4, :actor/robotics? true, :actor/coordination? true, :actor/proposal-ops [:log-case-file-record :schedule-interview-appointment :flag-investigation-review :coordinate-supply-order], :actor/always-escalate-ops [:flag-investigation-review], :actor/hard-checks [:officer-verified :effect-propose :op-not-allowed :case-file-basis :evidentiary-interpretation-forbidden :interview-substance-forbidden :scope-exclusion], :actor/scope-excluded-ops [:make-arrest :authorize-arrest :authorize-search :authorize-seizure :conduct-search :execute-search-warrant :file-formal-charge :file-charges :determine-guilt :determine-culpability :confirm-suspect-guilty], :actor/scope-excluded-terms ["make the arrest" "made the arrest" "execute the arrest" "executed the arrest" "authorize the arrest" "authorized the arrest" "issue the arrest warrant" "issued the arrest warrant" "authorize the search" "authorized the search" "authorize the seizure" "authorized the seizure" "conduct the search" "conducted the search" "execute the search warrant" "executed the search warrant" "file the formal charge" "filed the formal charge" "file formal charges" "filed formal charges" "file the charge" "filed the charge" "determine the suspect's guilt" "determined the suspect's guilt" "determine guilt" "determined guilt" "determine culpability" "determined culpability" "confirm the suspect's guilt" "confirmed the suspect's guilt" "establish the suspect's guilt" "established the suspect's guilt" "逮捕した" "逮捕を執行した" "逮捕状を発行した" "捜索を許可した" "差押えを許可した" "起訴した" "正式に起訴した" "有罪と断定した" "容疑者の有罪を確定した" "有罪を確定した"], :actor/cost-threshold-escalate-ops "{:coordinate-supply-order 500}", :phase/rollout "{0 {:label \"read-only\", :writes #{}, :auto #{}}, 1 {:label \"assisted-logging\", :writes #{:log-case-file-record}, :auto #{}}, 2 {:label \"assisted-coordination\", :writes #{:log-case-file-record :schedule-interview-appointment :coordinate-supply-order}, :auto #{}}, 3 {:label \"supervised-auto\", :writes #{:log-case-file-record :schedule-interview-appointment :coordinate-supply-order :flag-investigation-review}, :auto #{:log-case-file-record :schedule-interview-appointment :coordinate-supply-order}}}", :operation/nodes [:intake :advise :govern :decide :request-approval :commit :hold], :operation/entry-point :intake, :registry/maturity :implemented, :registry/required-technologies [:robotics :identity :audit-ledger], :registry/operating-states [:intake :propose :approve :execute :audit], :registry/repo "https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-3355", :registry/business-id "cloud-itonami-isco-3355", :test/counts "{:total 44, :assertions 144, :failures 0, :errors 0}", :test/coverage [:governor-hard-checks :advisor-shapes :integration :store-contract :scope-exclusion-self-trip-regression :officer-verification :case-verification :closed-op-allowlist :supply-cost-threshold-escalation :evidentiary-interpretation-forbidden :interview-substance-forbidden :rogue-advisor-end-to-end], :test/simulator :caseadmin.actor-test, :db/id -1, :adr/body "# ADR 2790003355: cloud-itonami ISCO-08 3355 Police Inspectors and Detectives case-file documentation/administrative-logistics coordination coverage\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nThis is part of the occupation-classification track (sibling to the\n`cloud-itonami-isic-*` industry-actor rollout, same governing\nADR-2607121000): codify every ISCO-08 occupation unit group as an\nautonomous \"actor\" (LLM/advisor behind an independent Governor, a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, append-only audit ledger), modeled on a\nrobotics premise -- a robot performs the occupation's physical/\nadministrative work, proposing actions to an independent Governor that\ngates them, never dispatches hardware itself, always escalates\nhigh-stakes decisions to a human. This ADR covers **ISCO-08 class 3355\n-- Police Inspectors and Detectives** only.\n\nThe `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's live `{:id \"3355\" ...}` entry\nwas verified against a fresh clone before any work began (`clojure -M\n-e \"(require 'kotoba.occupation) (println (kotoba.occupation/get-\noccupation \\\"3355\\\"))\"` from a checkout with the `kotoba-lang/\ntechnology` sibling present at the correct `../technology` relative\npath), and its `:name` read exactly \"Police Inspectors and Detectives\"\n-- confirming the premise, no mismatch. Prior to this ADR the entry's\n`:maturity` was `:spec` with `:required-technologies [:robotics\n:identity :audit-ledger]` and no `:repo`/`:business-id`; no repository\nexisted at `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-3355` (`gh api` 404 and\n`gh repo view` GraphQL both confirmed before scaffolding). This ADR and\nits companion registry edit promote the `3355` entry to `:implemented`.\n\n**This is the highest-stakes occupation actor built in this fleet's\nsession so far.** Police Inspectors and Detectives conduct criminal\ninvestigations, may have arrest authority, and operate in a domain\nwhere wrong autonomous action could cause someone's wrongful\ndetention, physical harm, or violation of due-process/civil rights --\na strictly more severe risk class than the fleet's prior most-cautious\nprecedent. That precedent is **ADR-2607152500** (Wave4 rollout start\namendment), which established that decisions directly touching a\nperson's safety, dignity or subsistence must always exclude the closed\nop allowlist and always escalate to a human, not merely be gated\nbehind a confidence threshold. The concurrent sibling\n`cloud-itonami-isco-3353` (Government Social Benefits Officials,\nlanded in this same batch) applied that guardrail to a\nbenefits-eligibility context. This ADR applies the identical guardrail\nshape to a domain with an even more severe failure mode: a wrongful\nbenefits denial is a serious, remediable harm; a wrongful arrest,\nsearch, or guilt determination can be an irreversible deprivation of\nphysical liberty and, in the worst case, physical safety. The guardrail\nhere is therefore held to at least the same strictness as\n`cloud-itonami-isco-3353`'s, with additional domain-specific\ndefense-in-depth described below.\n\nThe reference implementation mirrored for module SHAPE is\n[`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-3313`](https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-3313)\n(Accounting Associate Professionals: `store`/`advisor`/`governor`/\n`actor` split, `langgraph.graph` StateGraph, full doc set). The\nreference mirrored for the closed-allowlist + registered-AND-verified\nprovenance + content-based scope-exclusion SAFETY PATTERN specifically\nis the concurrent sibling\n[`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-3353`](https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-3353)\n(Government Social Benefits Officials) -- both independently re-cloned\nand re-read in full in this session, adapted substantially to the\narrest/search/charge/guilt-determination guardrail described below\nrather than following either reference's domain shape directly.\n\n## Decision\n\nPublish `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-3355` as an OSS\ndocumentation/logistics-coordination actor for police inspectors and\ndetectives, following the SAME governed-actor architecture as every\nprior `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actor in this fleet: **Case File Advisor\n⊣ CaseAdminGovernor** on a `langgraph.graph` StateGraph\n(`io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph`, git-sha-pinned identically to the\nreference's `deps.edn` -- this is a different library coordinate from\nthe `langgraph-clj` used by the unrelated `20-actors/*` actor family),\nwith an independent Governor, human-in-the-loop approval via\n`interrupt-before`, and an append-only audit ledger.\n\nThis actor is deliberately **case-file documentation and\nadministrative-logistics coordination ONLY, never investigative-\nconclusion or enforcement authority** -- it must NEVER be designed to\nexercise, simulate exercising, or propose exercising ANY of: an\narrest, a use-of-force decision, a search/seizure authorization, a\nformal accusation/charging decision, or a determination of a suspect's\nguilt or culpability. These are not merely gated behind escalation --\nthey are structurally absent from the op-allowlist entirely.\n\n### Closed proposal-op allowlist (all `:effect :propose`)\n\n- `:log-case-file-record` -- evidence-metadata/chain-of-custody entry\n  (physical handling log only -- item, timestamp, custodian chain --\n  NEVER an evidentiary interpretation or conclusion)\n- `:schedule-interview-appointment` -- witness/suspect interview\n  appointment scheduling proposal (never conducts or summarizes the\n  interview's substance)\n- `:flag-investigation-review` -- surface a case file that needs human\n  detective/inspector review (new case, evidence-intake trigger,\n  deadline), ALWAYS escalates immediately, NEVER auto-commit-eligible\n- `:coordinate-supply-order` -- forensic/office-equipment procurement\n  proposal\n\nThis actor has **NO op, anywhere in its allowlist, that resembles**:\nmaking an arrest, authorizing a search or seizure, filing a formal\ncharge, or determining a suspect's guilt or culpability. These are\n**structurally absent from the op-allowlist entirely**, not merely\ngated behind escalation -- an op such as `:make-arrest` cannot even be\nproposed by the reference mock advisor (its `infer` function only ever\nemits one of the four allowlist ops, driven by a `case` expression with\nno default branch producing any other op shape), and if any code path\n(a forged proposal, a future LLM advisor, a misbehaving fork) ever\nproduced such an op, the governor's closed-allowlist HARD check\n(`:op-not-allowed`) rejects it unconditionally and permanently.\nVerified two ways: (a) unit tests directly against `governor/check` for\neleven concretely-named forbidden op fixtures\n(`caseadmin.governor/scope-excluded-ops`: `:make-arrest`,\n`:authorize-arrest`, `:authorize-search`, `:authorize-seizure`,\n`:conduct-search`, `:execute-search-warrant`, `:file-formal-charge`,\n`:file-charges`, `:determine-guilt`, `:determine-culpability`,\n`:confirm-suspect-guilty`), and (b) an END-TO-END test that drives each\nof those same eleven ops through a ROGUE advisor and the FULL\n`langgraph.graph` actor graph (not just the governor's pure check\nfunction), proving the StateGraph itself always resolves to `:hold`\nwith zero records committed even when the advisor node itself is\ncompromised\n(`caseadmin.actor-test/holds-every-scope-excluded-op-attempt-even-via-a-rogue-advisor`).\n\n### Seven HARD governor checks (permanent, un-overridable)\n\n1. **Officer unregistered/unverified** -- any proposal must resolve to\n   an independently `:registered?`/`:verified?` officer record. Never\n   trusts the proposal's own claim of who the officer is. This directly\n   implements the task's \"officer/precinct record must be independently\n   verified/registered before any action\" invariant -- the officer\n   record itself carries `:precinct-id`, so officer verification and\n   precinct affiliation are checked together, not as two separate\n   entity lookups.\n2. **Effect not `:propose`** -- any other `:effect` value is a HARD\n   block (a claim to directly actuate outside governance).\n3. **Op not allowed** -- any `:op` outside the closed four-op allowlist\n   is a HARD, PERMANENT block. This independently rejects any attempt\n   to slip in a `:make-arrest`/`:authorize-search`/`:file-formal-charge`/\n   `:determine-guilt`-shaped op.\n4. **Case-file basis** -- `:log-case-file-record`,\n   `:schedule-interview-appointment` and `:coordinate-supply-order`\n   must cite a REGISTERED AND VERIFIED case belonging to the officer's\n   own precinct (`:missing-case-id` / `:unknown-case` /\n   `:case-unverified` / `:case-wrong-precinct`). `:flag-investigation-\n   review` is deliberately EXEMPT from this check -- it is the channel\n   by which a brand-new, not-yet-registered case is surfaced for human\n   intake, so it must not be blocked on the very case record it exists\n   to help create.\n5. **Evidentiary-interpretation forbidden** -- `:log-case-file-record`\n   is a physical chain-of-custody / metadata record ONLY (item,\n   timestamp, custodian chain). Any proposal carrying an evidentiary-\n   conclusion field (`:conclusion`, `:finding`, `:guilt`,\n   `:culpability`, `:determination`, `:suspect-identified`,\n   `:evidentiary-interpretation`, `:suspect-guilty?`) is a HARD,\n   PERMANENT block -- this actor never records an interpretation of\n   evidence, only its physical handling. This check is UNIQUE to this\n   ADR relative to the `cloud-itonami-isco-3353` reference -- the\n   benefits-documentation domain did not need an equivalent, but the\n   evidence-integrity risk here (a \"documentation\" op silently carrying\n   an investigative conclusion) required it.\n6. **Interview-substance forbidden** -- `:schedule-interview-\n   appointment` is scheduling logistics ONLY. Any proposal carrying\n   interview-content fields (`:summary`, `:statement`, `:testimony`,\n   `:confession`, `:interview-notes`, `:interview-summary`,\n   `:interviewee-statement`) is a HARD, PERMANENT block -- this actor\n   never conducts or summarizes an interview. Also UNIQUE to this ADR\n   relative to the reference, for the same reason as check 5.\n7. **Scope exclusion** -- independent of the op-allowlist check and\n   checks 5/6, any proposal whose free text (`:rationale` or `:note`)\n   names a finalization/execution action for an arrest, search/seizure\n   authorization, formal charge, or guilt/culpability determination\n   (e.g. \"made the arrest\", \"authorized the search\", \"filed the formal\n   charge\", \"determined the suspect's guilt\", plus Japanese\n   equivalents) is a HARD, PERMANENT block, evaluated unconditionally\n   on content. This is defense-in-depth on top of checks 3/5/6: even if\n   a future change somehow widened the allowlist or an allowed op's\n   field shape, content-based rejection still independently blocks\n   enforcement/investigative-conclusion language wherever it appears in\n   free text.\n\n### One always-escalate (SOFT) gate, one threshold gate, plus the general confidence floor\n\n- `:flag-investigation-review` -- ALWAYS escalates to a human,\n  regardless of confidence (governor's `always-escalate-ops`). This is\n  the ONLY channel by which the robot may surface an observation\n  suggesting a case needs human detective/inspector attention -- it\n  never resolves the observation itself, and the robot's role ends at\n  \"here is an organized case file,\" never \"here is what I think\n  happened\" or \"here is who did it.\"\n- a `:coordinate-supply-order` proposal whose `:cost` exceeds\n  `supply-cost-escalation-threshold` (500, inclusive boundary verified\n  by `ok-at-exact-supply-cost-threshold-boundary`) -- always needs\n  human sign-off, independent of confidence. This is an ESCALATION, not\n  a hard block: an over-budget forensic/office-equipment order is not\n  itself unsafe, unlike an arrest/search/charge/guilt-determination\n  attempt, which is why it is handled by a different mechanism (soft\n  escalate vs. structural absence).\n- (advisor confidence below `confidence-floor` 0.6 also escalates, for\n  any op.)\n\n### Self-trip guard (fleet-known bug class, carried over from the sibling ISIC/ISCO tracks)\n\nA governor's scope-exclusion term list phrased as a bare noun (e.g.\n\"arrest\", \"guilt\", \"charge\") can accidentally match inside the mock\nadvisor's own default rationale text for a legitimate proposal,\nself-blocking the actor's own happy path -- this is exactly the risk\nthis vertical's own vocabulary (every proposal necessarily discusses\ncase/officer/investigation concepts to do its documentation job) could\ntrigger if phrased carelessly. `caseadmin.governor/scope-excluded-\nterms` is phrased exclusively as finalization/execution ACTIONS (e.g.\n\"make the arrest\", \"authorize the search\", \"determine the suspect's\nguilt\", \"file the formal charge\"), never bare nouns, and\n`caseadmin.governor-test/default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-\ntrip-scope-exclusion` is a dedicated regression test asserting every\nop in the closed allowlist (including both the case-id-present and\ncase-id-nil variants of `:flag-investigation-review`), driven through\nthe default mock advisor, never trips `:scope-excluded` or\n`:op-not-allowed`. The mock advisor's own default rationale template\n(\"documented <op> for case <id>\" / \"documented <op> (no case yet --\nnew-case intake)\") was written to avoid any bare-noun collision by\nconstruction. Green on first run in this session -- no self-trip was\nactually hit during development, but this ADR still documents the\nguard and its regression test since the risk class is especially acute\nfor this domain's vocabulary.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's `{:id \"3355\" ...}` entry promoted\n  from `:spec` to `:implemented`, with `:repo`/`:business-id` set to\n  the real repository\n  (`https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-3355` /\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-3355`), and `maturity-summary`'s implemented\n  count bumped accordingly (recomputed live from the registry via\n  `kotoba.occupation/maturity-summary`, not assumed, immediately before\n  the edit to account for concurrent sibling landings in this same\n  batch).\n- Full test suite (`clojure -M:test`): 44 tests, 144 assertions, 0\n  failures, 0 errors -- raw output captured in this ADR's\n  `:test/counts` and in the task report, independently re-verified\n  against a brand-new fresh clone of the pushed repository (not just\n  the local working copy).\n- `clj-kondo` lint of `src`/`test`: 0 errors, 0 warnings (ad hoc run;\n  this actor's `deps.edn` does not define a `:lint` alias, matching the\n  verified `cloud-itonami-isco-3313` reference's own drift -- see Notes\n  below).\n- No `manifest/west.yml` changes -- this actor is registered purely via\n  the `kotoba-lang/occupation` capability registry, consistent with\n  sibling `cloud-itonami-isco-*`/`cloud-itonami-isic-*` actors.\n- No `kotoba-lang/technology` dependency was added to the actor's\n  `deps.edn` -- consistent with the live convention already confirmed\n  by sibling ISCO actors this batch (`cloud-itonami-isco-3313`/`-3353`\n  do NOT depend on `kotoba-lang/technology`; only the central\n  `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry itself depends on it, to resolve\n  `:required-technologies` stacks).\n- This ADR is EDN-only, matching the live `90-docs/adr` convention\n  (commit `6d2d0eeda658`, \"Remove all .md, normalize ADRs to tx-data\")\n  -- a single-entity EDN vector with an `:adr/body` string blob rather\n  than a paired `.md`+`.edn`.\n- `CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md`/`SECURITY.md` say \"cloud-itonami organization\"\n  for private-contact routing (the reference `cloud-itonami-isco-3313`\n  repo and the concurrent `cloud-itonami-isco-3353` sibling both say\n  \"gftdcojp organization,\" which is stale since both are published\n  under `cloud-itonami`) -- this repo uses the factually-correct org\n  name, matching the fix independently made by the `cloud-itonami-\n  isco-3344` sibling earlier in this same batch.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- Giving the actor an op like `:approve-arrest`/`:authorize-search`\n  that is merely gated behind `always-escalate-ops` (the shape\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-3313` uses for `:approve-over-ceiling-posting`,\n  or the shape a naive reading of \"gate high-stakes actions behind\n  human approval\" might suggest): rejected outright per the explicit\n  task guidance, the `ADR-2607152500` precedent, and the\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-3353` precedent -- an always-escalate op still\n  means the *capability* to make an arrest/authorize a search/file a\n  charge/determine guilt exists in the code path and is merely deferred\n  to a human gate. For a decision this severe (irreversible deprivation\n  of physical liberty, potential physical harm, due-process violation),\n  the capability itself must not exist. The only op related to\n  investigative escalation is `:flag-investigation-review`, which\n  surfaces the need for a human decision and never itself decides,\n  authorizes, or defers an enforcement action for later automatic\n  execution.\n- A bare-noun scope-exclusion term list (e.g. `[\"arrest\" \"guilt\"\n  \"charge\" \"search\"]`): rejected outright per the fleet-known self-trip\n  bug class described above -- this actor's own domain necessarily\n  discusses case/investigation concepts to do its documentation job, so\n  a bare-noun list would risk self-blocking the actor's own legitimate\n  proposals (e.g. logging evidence \"related to the ongoing\n  investigation\" would false-positive on a bare \"investigation\" or\n  case-related term if phrased carelessly; the actual implementation\n  avoids this by using full finalization/execution action phrases).\n- Merging `officer` and `case-file` into a single entity (only checking\n  one provenance record): rejected -- the cross-precinct check\n  (`:case-wrong-precinct`) requires two independently registered-AND-\n  verified entities so that a case belonging to a different precinct\n  than the proposing officer is caught even if both records individually\n  pass verification, matching the two-entity provenance shape already\n  established by `cloud-itonami-isco-3353`'s applicant+office pattern.\n- Allowing `:schedule-interview-appointment` to carry a brief interview\n  OUTCOME field (e.g. a `:completed?`/`:no-show?` status, as distinct\n  from interview *substance*): considered, but rejected for this\n  initial implementation -- even a status-only field is a plausible\n  seed for scope creep into recording interview content over time\n  (a \"completed\" flag today, a \"completed with statement attached\"\n  field tomorrow). Scheduling logistics only for v1; a follow-up ADR\n  could reintroduce a narrowly-scoped, explicitly content-free status\n  field if a legitimate administrative need is demonstrated, with its\n  own dedicated forbidden-keys guardrail.\n- A numeric confidence-only gate for `:log-case-file-record` /\n  `:schedule-interview-appointment` (no forbidden-keys content check):\n  rejected as insufficient -- confidence measures the advisor's\n  certainty about the *proposal it chose to make*, not whether that\n  proposal smuggles forbidden content; a high-confidence advisor could\n  still misuse an allowed op's field shape to carry a forbidden\n  evidentiary conclusion or interview statement, which is exactly why\n  checks 5/6 exist as independent, content-based, permanent HARD\n  blocks regardless of confidence.\n\n## Itemized safety confirmation\n\nEvery op in this actor's closed proposal-op allowlist, and why it is\nsafe under the constraints above:\n\n1. **`:log-case-file-record`** -- physical evidence-handling metadata\n   only (item id, timestamp, custodian, chain-of-custody). Cannot carry\n   an evidentiary interpretation or conclusion (HARD-blocked by check\n   5, `:evidentiary-interpretation-forbidden`, on a closed forbidden-key\n   list: `:conclusion`, `:finding`, `:guilt`, `:culpability`,\n   `:determination`, `:suspect-identified`, `:evidentiary-\n   interpretation`, `:suspect-guilty?`). Not an arrest, search, charge,\n   or guilt determination in any respect -- it is a records-management\n   action indistinguishable in kind from a librarian's accession log.\n2. **`:schedule-interview-appointment`** -- appointment logistics only\n   (interviewee role, proposed time, location). Cannot carry interview\n   substance or conclusions (HARD-blocked by check 6,\n   `:interview-substance-forbidden`, on a closed forbidden-key list:\n   `:summary`, `:statement`, `:testimony`, `:confession`, `:interview-\n   notes`, `:interview-summary`, `:interviewee-statement`). Does not\n   conduct, summarize, or draw any conclusion from an interview -- it\n   is a calendar action.\n3. **`:flag-investigation-review`** -- surfaces a case file to a human\n   detective/inspector; ALWAYS escalates (governor's `always-escalate-\n   ops`, unconditionally, at every confidence level), NEVER auto-commit\n   eligible. Carries only administrative trigger metadata (`:reason`\n   from a closed keyword set, `:note` free text subject to the same\n   scope-exclusion check as every other op's free text). This is the\n   ONLY channel through which an investigative observation may be\n   surfaced, and it explicitly never resolves, decides, or concludes\n   anything itself -- the human reviews and acts entirely on their own\n   authority.\n4. **`:coordinate-supply-order`** -- forensic/office-equipment\n   procurement proposal (item, cost, vendor). Not an enforcement or\n   investigative action of any kind -- it is a purchasing-logistics\n   action, gated by ordinary cost-ceiling escalation (above 500 always\n   escalates) like any office procurement workflow.\n\nNo op in this allowlist, and no op anywhere in this codebase, resembles\nan arrest, a use-of-force decision, a search/seizure authorization, a\nformal accusation/charging decision, or a determination of a suspect's\nguilt or culpability -- these five categories are structurally absent,\nnot gated, confirmed by: (a) the closed four-op allowlist itself\n(`caseadmin.governor/closed-op-allowlist`), (b) eleven concretely-named\nforbidden-op fixtures that are rejected at both the governor-unit level\nand the full-actor-graph level via a rogue advisor\n(`caseadmin.governor/scope-excluded-ops`,\n`caseadmin.governor-test/every-scope-excluded-op-name-is-rejected`,\n`caseadmin.actor-test/holds-every-scope-excluded-op-attempt-even-via-a-\nrogue-advisor`), (c) a content-based scope-exclusion check independent\nof the `:op` field (`caseadmin.governor/out-of-scope?`,\n`caseadmin.governor/scope-excluded-terms`), and (d) two additional\ncontent-shape guardrails unique to this domain preventing an\notherwise-allowed op from smuggling forbidden substance through its own\nfield shape (checks 5/6 above).\n"}]
